  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `.github/workflows/aur-package.yml` compiles nothing now. It downloads the `linux-packages` artifact of the same run. It unpacks `camcraft-ui`, `camcraft-cli` and `post` from `camcraft-<version>-linux-x86_64.tar.gz`.\n- `makepkg -o --noprepare -d` gets, checks and extracts the recipe source. Then `makepkg -R -d` runs only `package()` around the prebuilt binaries.\n- A CI copy of the recipe (`PKGBUILD.prebuilt`, not committed) adds `'!strip' '!debug'`. makepkg then does not change the binaries.\n- A new check compares the SHA256 of each packaged binary with the binary in the Linux tarball. A difference fails the job. On a tag run, the tarball version must agree with the tag.\n- A dispatch run packages the assets of its own checkout, because its binaries come from that checkout.\n- The job installs only `base-devel` and `curl`. It installs no Rust and no library headers.\n- `aur/PKGBUILD` and `aur/.SRCINFO` do not change. They stay the from-source recipe for AUR users. The `.SRCINFO` check still runs.\n- `release.yml`: one comment line on the `aur` job. No trigger and no `on:` block changed.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3773-aur-reuse-linux.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Tag run 45269109413 (v0.25.0): `aur / build` ran 21:42:18 -> 22:31:11, that is 48 min 53 s, about 49 billed Linux minutes.\n- `publish` waited for the AUR job for 30 minutes after the last other platform (macOS ended at 22:01:16).\n- Expected after: about 2-4 minutes (container pull, `pacman -Syu base-devel curl`, artifact download, `makepkg -R`). Expected saving: about 45 billed minutes for each tag run. The release page goes out about 30 minutes earlier.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Both workflow files parse as YAML (`yaml.safe_load`).\n- Each `run:` script of the AUR job passes `bash -n`.\n- The `options=` sed edit was run on `aur/PKGBUILD`. It gives `options=('!lto' '!strip' '!debug')`, and the guard `grep` matches.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The job did not run. A `workflow_dispatch` of `release.yml` without `site_only` builds all platforms, which is a full release run. `site_only` skips `linux` and thus `aur`. No Docker is on this machine for a local Arch container run.\n- The first real run is the next tag run, or a dispatch that the maintainer starts.\n\nThis is a `.github` change. It waits for the maintainer's read (`needs-maintainer`).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: medium\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3773\n",
